WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.708
An ablation isolates the consistency loss.

00:00:03.788 --> 00:00:07.497
Across training-set sizes of five thousand,
twenty-five hundred,

00:00:07.577 --> 00:00:11.285
and one thousand samples,

00:00:11.365 --> 00:00:15.073
adding the consistency loss consistently improves
both accuracy and the scale-consistency rate.

00:00:15.153 --> 00:00:18.862
For example,

00:00:18.942 --> 00:00:22.650
at five thousand samples the scale-consistency
rises from ninety-one and a half percent

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:26.438
to nearly ninety-three percent.

00:00:26.518 --> 00:00:30.227
This confirms that the hinge consistency loss is
doing real work,

00:00:30.307 --> 00:00:34.015
encouraging the model to make better predictions as
resolution increases.

00:00:34.095 --> 00:00:37.803
The authors also note that applying the
non-linearity directly in the frequency domain,

00:00:37.883 --> 00:00:41.592
though equivariant, hurt classification,

00:00:41.672 --> 00:00:45.380
which is why they designed the spatial-domain
scale-equivariant non-linearity.
